From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:47:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-9: WPF-style editing -- drag, resize handles,
 arrow nudge, editable property grid, written into the HTML source (0.9.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User 20260929: "用你覺得合理的一直做下去 只要操作上跟WPF一樣就好".

- design surface: press = select (WPF), drag = move, 8 handles = resize,
  arrows = 1px (Shift 10px), Ctrl+arrows = resize, Esc = parent, Tab /
  Shift+Tab = next / previous, Enter = default event; Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y / Ctrl+S
  are VS Code's own (the page is a normal TextDocument)
- properties panel "外觀與版面（可編輯）": Left Top Width Height Caption/Text
  Visible Enabled Font.Size Font.Color Color, commit on Enter / leaving the field
- lib/htmledit.js: the exact characters to change -- one declaration of one
  start tag's style (in place; spaces and order kept), one attribute, or one
  caption text (button / label / <legend> / Panel caption / input value).
  Anchoring kept: left+width, left+right, right+width. An <input> moves its
  positioning <span>. Non-px values and JS-built controls are refused, not guessed
- one edit = one WorkspaceEdit = one undo step (a burst of arrow keys is one);
  edits are queued per page; the designer's own edits do not reload the page,
  undo does. Nothing is saved to disk by the extension; a first-edit notice says
  the page is synced by sync_web.py (--apply overwrites) and warns about autoSave
- DFM and BCB6 stay read-only

Tests: lib 84 (incl. byte-for-byte add/remove, in-place style edits) / probe
2 pages x 16 now asserted (drag, handles, nudge, wrapper, Esc, Tab, caption) /
fake vscode 52 (source edits, escaping, queueing, refusal, nothing else changed)
+ panels 10 / real VS Code 48: Left=60 -> source + dirty -> Ctrl+Z twice ->
exact original -> re-render; never saved, opened files byte-identical (MD5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
